{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"congruent-demurrable-insect","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nDuring a compaction fold, `_build_authorship_ledger` -> `authorship.identify_signer` -> `_keyring_for` -> `rebar.show_ticket` -> `ensure_fresh` runs while `_compact_locked` holds the store write lock. When the 60 s freshness marker has expired, `ensure_fresh` runs `git fetch` (network in production) and then `sync.reconverge`, which requests the same store write lock the fold already holds. It waits out its 2 s pass against its own process, then gives up.\n\nMeasured on a clone of `tickets` at `daa3a65239b^` with a local mirror as `origin` (2026-11-03, `origin/main` `25bce6c0550`): first signed fold `ensure_fresh` 2.22 s, nested lock wait 2.04 s, fetch 0.11 s (local mirror; production fetches over the network). Evidence on `breezelike-travelsick-moray`.\n\n## Expected\nA locked critical section never fetches and never requests a lock it already holds. Keyring lookups for the ledger read local state, or run before the lock like `preresolve_unmapped_positions`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A fold with signed events runs no `git fetch` and no store-lock acquisition while `_compact_locked` holds the lock (test observes the lock dir at each call).\n- [ ] The authorship ledger is unchanged for the same input.","id":"1ae0-ff59-b62e-4267","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A compaction fold fetches and re-requests its own lock inside the lock"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793718359512175001,"uuid":"69b56e16-972a-442f-a824-bbc415b0533e"}